Package: mlmr
Title: A Guided Interface for Mixed-Effects and Multilevel Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Marcus", "Harris", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "marcus.harris.uconn@gmail.com")
Description: Provides a guided HLM-style Shiny interface and reusable R helpers
    for specifying, fitting, explaining, and reporting mixed-effects and
    multilevel models with 'lme4' (Bates, Maechler, Bolker, and Walker, 2015,
    <doi:10.18637/jss.v067.i01>). Supports grand-mean and cluster-mean centering
    (Enders and Tofighi, 2007, <doi:10.1037/1082-989X.12.2.121>), nested,
    longitudinal, and crossed random-effects structures, cross-level slope
    moderation, optional Satterthwaite and Kenward-Roger denominator degrees of
    freedom via 'lmerTest' (Kuznetsova, Brockhoff, and Christensen, 2017,
    <doi:10.18637/jss.v082.i13>), Huber-White cluster-robust sandwich standard
    errors, empirical Bayes random-coefficient reliabilities, variance-component
    likelihood-ratio and homogeneity tests (Raudenbush and Bryk, 2002,
    ISBN:9780761919049), marginal and conditional R-squared (Nakagawa, Johnson,
    and Schielzeth, 2017, <doi:10.1098/rsif.2017.0213>), live pre-fit and fitted
    equations, APA-style tables, diagnostics, and reproducible publication
    archive bundles.
